 "tint": {
  "_comment": "A tinted garment keeps its texture's light and dark (contrast 1 = all of it) around the new colour, each texel held within 1/max_ratio..max_ratio of the mean. A connected piece of a garment is its bottom when its mean height is under split_height_frac of the body's height or it reaches below legwear_below_frac (about the knee); every other piece is its top.",
  "contrast": 0.85,
  "split_height_frac": 0.5,
  "legwear_below_frac": 0.3,
  "max_ratio": 2.0,
  "mask_dilate_px": 3
 },
 "skin_tone_strength": 1.0,
 "_comment_skin_normal": "The skin's normal map, derived from its own colour map (openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-29-character-lighting): the luminance less its blur over blur_px source pixels is the height, and strength scales its slope. At 16 the median tilt is 3 degrees and the 95th percentile 15 (measured on middleage_african_male): pores, not stone.",
 "skin_normal": {
  "blur_px": 6.0,
  "strength": 16.0
 },
 "_comment_skin_roughness": "How rough skin is where (make_skin_roughness.py paints it into npc_skin_roughness.png, MakeHuman UV): the T-zone (forehead, nose, lips) oily, the cheeks and chin less, the rest dry; blurred over blur_px so the areas blend.",
 "skin_roughness": {
  "t_zone": 0.42,
  "cheeks": 0.55,
  "body": 0.62,
  "blur_px": 6.0
 },
 "_comment_outfit_roughness": "How rough the outfit material is, in its normal map's alpha (openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-29-character-lighting, design section 8): the eyes share the outfit's atlas and material, so their tile is wet (a catchlight from the key) and the clothes and gear are cloth.",
